{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>For she covered her face.</b> Its meaning is ותתעלף (and she acted as a harlot). The one who explains כי כסתה פניה as referring to kinds of cosmetics, and brings proof from her daughter — that is vain, for one does not bring proof from fools. Also correct is what the Rabbis of blessed memory expounded, that she was modest in her father-in-law's house."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 38, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:47:24.263149616Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}